      "message": "I think this `copy()` approach is a bit too invasive; it requires us to implement `copy()` for each existing type and maintain it in the future.\n\nSeems a lot of code, imho.\n\nI liked better the original approach you suggested:\n\n\n```\nif (message instanceof MultiSiteEvent multiSiteEvent) {\n  MultiSiteEvent requeuedEvent \u003d\n      (MultiSiteEvent) gson.fromJson(gson.toJson(multiSiteEvent), Event.class);\n  requeuedEvent.markRequeued(nodeInstanceId);\n  return send(topic, requeuedEvent, MessageLogger.Direction.REQUEUE);\n}\nreturn send(topic, message, MessageLogger.Direction.REQUEUE);\n```\n\nThe `EventDeserializer` should do the right thing and preserve the specifics of the `MultiSiteEvent` (`ChangeIndexEvent`, `CacheEvictionEvent`), because we called `MultiSiteEvent.registerEventTypes()`.\n\nCan you just add a test covering this case to make sure the requeued object is the expected one? Especially around `CacheEvictionEvent.key` which is declared as `Object`.",
